\"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794255945153072001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2b81edf7-9d9c-4b35-8243-837824e3dee1","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"75af-1212-aa22-463f"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe point of a second engine is to compare it with the first. The epic requires a harness that runs both engines on the same ticket and ref and reports verdict agreement and finding overlap, run once over rebar's own eval corpus (`evals/`).\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd an operator-run harness, `src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py`, modelled on the existing operator harness `provider_parity.py` (same CLI shape, `--dry-run`, `--limit`, `--out`, never a CI job). For each corpus item it calls `review_plan(..., engine=\"pipeline\", sign=False)` and `review_plan(..., engine=\"agentic\", sign=False)` at the same ref, and reports: verdict agreement (exact PASS/BLOCK/INDETERMINATE match rate and the confusion matrix), blocking-decision flips, and finding overlap (findings matched by criterion and normalized text through `sidecar.norm_id`/`fix_unit_key`, `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py:303,321`; reported as matched, pipeline-only and agentic-only counts). Corpus: the gold-labelled plan-review cases the parity harness already selects (`provider_parity.eligible_cases`/`select_corpus`), so both harnesses read one corpus definition. Results are written as JSON beside `provider_parity_results.json` and summarized in a ticket comment on the epic, with no cost figures. Reusing the parity harness's corpus selection and shape keeps the evidence comparable and avoids a second corpus definition.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py (new)\n- src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/engine_comparison_results.json (recorded run)\n- tests/unit/test_engine_comparison.py (new)\n- docs/llm-framework.md (how to run it)\n\n## Testing\n\n- With `FakeRunner` scripted per engine: identical verdicts give agreement 1.0; one flipped item gives the expected confusion matrix; overlap counts match a hand-computed worked example (2 shared, 1 pipeline-only, 1 agentic-only).\n- `--dry-run` lists the corpus and makes no model call.\n- An item that errors on one engine is counted as an error, not as a disagreement.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_engine_comparison.py` passes, pinning agreement, confusion matrix, overlap and error handling.\n- [ ] One run over the eval corpus is recorded in `engine_comparison_results.json` and summarized in a comment on the epic.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py","reason":"new harness"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/engine_comparison_results.json","reason":"recorded run"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_engine_comparison.py","reason":"new tests"},{"path":"docs/llm-framework.md","reason":"how to run"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","75af-1212-aa22-463f"],["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b690-7231-22fe-49e4","ticket_type":"story","title":"Engine comparison harness: verdict agreement and finding overlap over the eval corpus","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["154796c1-9d6b-44f1-85de-03e8f7b261f0","2b81edf7-9d9c-4b35-8243-837824e3dee1","8ded56be-38bb-461e-b775-e5708a395d1d"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794260922621599002,"uuid":"f869ba49-f241-4347-922c-d02c4e898bdb"}